// Title: Suspicious Invocation of Shell via AWK - Linux
// Sigma ID: 8c1a5675-cb85-452f-a298-b01b22a51856
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Li Ling, Andy Parkidomo, Robert Rakowski, Blake Hartstein (Bloomberg L.P.)
// Date: 2024-09-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects the execution of "awk" or it's sibling commands, to invoke a shell using the system()
//   function. This behavior is commonly associated with attempts to execute arbitrary commands or
//   escalate privileges, potentially leading to unauthorized access or further exploitation.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/awk/#shell
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/gawk/#shell
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/nawk/#shell
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/mawk/#shell
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_awk_shell_spawn.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "/awk" or FolderPath endswith "/gawk" or FolderPath endswith "/mawk" or FolderPath endswith "/nawk") and ProcessCommandLine contains "BEGIN {system") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/dash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/fish" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/zsh")
